# Real scientific functions with checked finite domains; all angles use radians.
let values be a list of 0, 1, 2.
let exponentials be map every x in values to (exp of x).
let logarithms be map every x in (a list of 1, 2, 4) to (ln of x).
assert exp of 0 is equal to 1.0.
assert ln of 1 is equal to 0.0.
assert sin of 0 is equal to 0.0.
assert cos of 0 is equal to 1.0.
assert log2 of 8 is equal to 3.0.
assert log10 of 100 is equal to 2.0.
assert asin of 0 is equal to 0.0.
assert acos of 1 is equal to 0.0.
assert atan of 0 is equal to 0.0.
assert length of exponentials is equal to 3.
assert length of logarithms is equal to 3.
let probabilities be a list of 0, 0.5, 1.
let angles be map every p in probabilities to (asin of p).
assert length of angles is equal to 3.
assert (angles at 2) is greater than 1.5.
assert (angles at 2) is less than 1.6.
print "scientific math OK".
